                    {
                        "translation_id": "241cd8f8-22a6-4966-ab5f-e3a5eddce842",
                        "source_entry_id": "16cfbae3-a8f3-3acc-b872-ee4818126575",
                        "source_sense_description": "Personne qui remplit plusieurs rôles",
                        "target_lang_word": "handyman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "handyman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cce9f378-207f-3e57-9ae0-dc1dc2073889",
                                        "entry_id": "823af978-d327-38a9-ae09-a19e873edac5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who does small tasks and odd jobs, especially building repairs and the like."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a74268b-384d-465b-a9ca-da0d5165ccf8",
                                                "sense_id": "cce9f378-207f-3e57-9ae0-dc1dc2073889",
                                                "text": "I complained that the heat was not working, and the landlord sent the handyman to fix it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62bb315a-0852-4fe8-a61f-b4c79827a8f5",
                                                "sense_id": "cce9f378-207f-3e57-9ae0-dc1dc2073889",
                                                "text": "There was one thing she wanted; she said to hubby dear, / \"The time would pass more quickly if I had a rocking chair.\" / [...] As Strings is such a handyman, by night the job was done / He took that thing upstairs and said, \"Now try this out for fun.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "handyman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eaa3ed77-bf5a-321e-80f8-7008601cba6a",
                                        "entry_id": "f79d5fe6-8e62-39c1-9b62-154543a62267",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To work as a handyman; to do odd jobs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62bd5c7a-341f-4af6-9177-781f77f47b79",
                                                "sense_id": "eaa3ed77-bf5a-321e-80f8-7008601cba6a",
                                                "text": "Instead I walk, uncertainly across the concrete backyard my father and his friends handymanned into existence so proudly, so that none of us would ever have to play in dirt, in muck, in mud again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e93b38c7-7273-4d37-9448-0b4a9c3ce33d",
                                                "sense_id": "eaa3ed77-bf5a-321e-80f8-7008601cba6a",
                                                "text": "My daddy worked too hard at Buck's Sporting Goods by day plus handymanning in the evenings, and my mother spent too many hours fixing trays at the meat-and-three for me to act like we had neither pot nor window. Let the record show that we had both."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbb43741-319c-474d-9a7d-0bf3b447b634",
                                                "sense_id": "eaa3ed77-bf5a-321e-80f8-7008601cba6a",
                                                "text": "They handymanned all week. And every night Grandad would come in with rosy cheeks and a huge appetite and compliment my mom on what a great cook she was."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "30af54df-2e4b-49d1-8921-7d65ba4c14d9",
                        "source_entry_id": "16cfbae3-a8f3-3acc-b872-ee4818126575",
                        "source_sense_description": "Personne qui remplit plusieurs rôles",
                        "target_lang_word": "jack of all trades",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jack of all trades",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4b2332d-4d9d-32b4-8baf-336cd702c4f5",
                                        "entry_id": "06ee170b-514f-3afe-b97e-97bc57f34a5f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One competent in many endeavours, sometimes regarded as not excelling in any of them."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2038f1cb-40f9-4add-ab36-7e56774c5c89",
                                                "sense_id": "e4b2332d-4d9d-32b4-8baf-336cd702c4f5",
                                                "text": "Novv for the moſt part your Porter is either ſome broken Cittizen, vvho hath plaid Iack of all trades, ſome Pander, Broker, or Hangman, that hath plaid the knaue vvith all men, and for the more certainty his Embleme is a red Beard, to vvhich Sacke hath made his Noſe couſin German."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14e7aa89-7087-4a0f-aff5-57d6e325c62e",
                                                "sense_id": "e4b2332d-4d9d-32b4-8baf-336cd702c4f5",
                                                "text": "Printer, postmaster, almanac maker, essayist, chemist, orator, tinker, statesman, humorist, philosopher, parlor man, political economist, professor of housewifery, ambassador, projector, maxim-monger, herb-doctor, wit:—Jack of all trades, master of each and mastered by none—the type and genius of his land."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dce0a0ce-f2b1-47f1-b5f6-92f17db576c8",
                                                "sense_id": "e4b2332d-4d9d-32b4-8baf-336cd702c4f5",
                                                "text": "\"I am my own engineer, and my own carpenter, and my own plumber, and my own gardener, and my own Jack of all Trades,\" said Wemmick, in acknowledging my compliments."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d63874e2-b499-49e2-b834-227b7d75d73f",
                                                "sense_id": "e4b2332d-4d9d-32b4-8baf-336cd702c4f5",
                                                "text": "A fellow can always get some sort of a job—I was coming up here to see if they needed an extra clerk or a waiter, or chauffeur, or anything that meant a roof and something to eat—but I suppose they don't need a jack-of-all-trades."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f07cbfdf-b61e-42c3-aa9b-118c204fe866",
                                                "sense_id": "e4b2332d-4d9d-32b4-8baf-336cd702c4f5",
                                                "text": "In 1823, when this drawing was made, there was anesthesia for dentistry and in fact very little dentistry except the extraction of teeth. Much of this extraction was conducted by itinerant quacks or jacks-of-all-trades who did it as a side line to their business."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
